Use strscpy() instead of strncpy() in the sysfs show handlers.

Linux 7.2 no longer declares strncpy() for modules, so every one of these
five calls is a hard "call to undeclared library function 'strncpy'" error.
strscpy() is the drop-in here: the destination is a PAGE_SIZE sysfs buffer,
the source is a small fixed array, and each caller already computes its own
length with strnlen() and appends the newline itself - the NUL padding
strncpy() did was never read. strscpy() has been available since 4.3, so
the patched source still builds against the older kernels in this overlay.

Not sent upstream: gitlab.com/ddcci-driver-linux has had no commit since
2025-09-27.
--- a/ddcci/ddcci.c
+++ b/ddcci/ddcci.c
@@ -765,7 +765,7 @@
 
 	if (likely(device != NULL)) {
 		len = strnlen(device->prot, sizeof(device->prot));
-		strncpy(buf, device->prot, PAGE_SIZE);
+		strscpy(buf, device->prot, PAGE_SIZE);
 		if (len == 0) {
 			ret = len;
 		} else if (likely(len < PAGE_SIZE)) {
@@ -787,7 +787,7 @@
 
